      "problem": "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-6x-2z+8=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-6x-2z+8 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-6x)+4{y}^{2}-({z}^{2}+2z)+8 & =0 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9+4{y}^{2}-(z+1)^{2}+1+8 & =0 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+4{y}^{2}-(z+1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an elliptic cone centered at $(3,0,-1).$",
